# Relative path, not an absolute URL - nginx.conf serves the built frontend
# and proxies /api on the SAME origin/port (80), so the browser always calls
# "wherever this page came from" + /api. This is deliberate: it means the
# built frontend keeps working even if the instance's public IP changes
# (see README.md's Elastic IP note) or you later put a domain in front of
# it - no rebuild needed either way.
VITE_API_URL=/api
